WEBVTT

00:01.740 --> 00:04.120
<i>I'm sorry to repeat myself so many times, but...</i>

00:10.530 --> 00:11.730
Nowaki...

00:12.250 --> 00:13.330
I'm cold...

00:14.000 --> 00:14.790
Yes.

00:15.770 --> 00:17.920
<i>...I think Hiro-san is really cute.</i>

00:19.520 --> 00:21.280
Your schedule tomorrow...?

00:21.650 --> 00:23.820
I have an afternoon shift at work.

00:24.040 --> 00:26.520
Ah, but I'll wake you up.

00:26.670 --> 00:27.520
It's okay.

00:27.640 --> 00:29.130
I'll wake up on my own.

00:29.560 --> 00:34.070
It's no problem. Tommorrow's my turn to make breakfast, anyway.

00:34.840 --> 00:36.620
Well, whatever.

00:39.270 --> 00:40.160
Good night.

00:45.040 --> 00:50.040
The mouth is the gate of misfortune

00:50.340 --> 00:55.590
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

00:50.340 --> 00:55.590
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

00:53.740 --> 01:07.010
Junjou Romantica 2

00:55.590 --> 00:59.060
ima futari no story

00:55.590 --> 00:59.060
Now, our story...

01:00.350 --> 01:07.840
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

01:00.350 --> 01:07.840
Our future is going to shine on.

01:11.280 --> 01:16.570
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

01:11.280 --> 01:16.570
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

01:17.040 --> 01:21.400
okubyou ni naru bakari

01:17.040 --> 01:21.400
and always lose my nerve.

01:21.400 --> 01:27.000
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

01:21.400 --> 01:27.000
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

01:27.000 --> 01:30.630
kimi to aeru nara

01:27.000 --> 01:30.630
if it means I can see you.

01:32.660 --> 01:37.640
ame ni utarete furueru koe

01:32.660 --> 01:37.640
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

01:37.970 --> 01:43.240
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

01:37.970 --> 01:43.240
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

01:43.920 --> 01:46.720
boku wa yuku yo

01:43.920 --> 01:46.720
I'll go,

01:46.720 --> 01:53.470
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

01:46.720 --> 01:53.470
Until the day when I can see you.

01:54.290 --> 01:59.480
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

01:54.290 --> 01:59.480
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

01:59.480 --> 02:03.190
ima futari no story

01:59.480 --> 02:03.190
Now, our story

02:03.350 --> 02:05.000
ugokidashita

02:03.350 --> 02:05.000
has started.

02:05.000 --> 02:09.990
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

02:05.000 --> 02:09.990
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

02:09.990 --> 02:17.180
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

02:09.990 --> 02:17.180
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

02:21.310 --> 02:23.830
Nowaki! You bastard!

02:24.490 --> 02:26.580
Didn't you say you'd wake me up!?

02:26.740 --> 02:28.190
I tried to...

02:28.530 --> 02:29.760
...about 20 times.

02:30.290 --> 02:33.040
Liar! I don't remember at all!

02:33.690 --> 02:35.440
Would you like to have some breakfast before going?

02:35.820 --> 02:37.660
Sorry, no time!

02:38.260 --> 02:38.940
Bye.

02:39.000 --> 02:40.260
Oh, Hiro-san...

02:50.090 --> 02:51.180
Have a good day.

02:56.640 --> 02:57.760
See you.

02:58.490 --> 03:00.430
Okay. Be careful...

03:01.900 --> 03:02.840
<i>Why is it...?</i>

03:06.530 --> 03:08.340
<i>Why does he make that kind of face?</i>

03:14.180 --> 03:16.400
<i>Actually, it's been worrying me for some time now...</i>

03:17.500 --> 03:22.440
<i>Hiro-san...Is he really happy to be living together with me?</i>

03:22.890 --> 03:25.610
<i>If he doesn't like something he says so straight away,</i>

03:25.850 --> 03:31.350
<i>so me being near him or touching him doesn't... bother him, I think.</i>

03:31.970 --> 03:34.410
<i>But, is he just being shy?</i>

03:39.480 --> 03:40.810
<i>Not possible.</i>

03:45.780 --> 03:47.980
<i>I managed to get us to live together, but</i>

03:48.910 --> 03:52.090
<i>it's not as if Hiro-san and my relationship has especially changed.</i>

03:52.880 --> 03:55.450
<i>Hiro-san is busy with his research at the University,</i>

03:56.080 --> 03:58.310
<i>and I just run back and forth between the hospital and my part-time job.</i>

04:01.390 --> 04:03.890
<i>There are also many days when we don't see each other.</i>

04:05.170 --> 04:09.090
<i>And I have no wish of intruding his private time.</i>

04:09.930 --> 04:10.580
<i>But...</i>

04:16.250 --> 04:17.190
<i>...it's just...</i>

04:17.820 --> 04:19.710
<i>Since we are finally living together,</i>

04:19.960 --> 04:21.960
<i>even if we don't get lovey-dovey with each other,</i>

04:22.000 --> 04:25.200
<i>if he could take some kind of action, it would be nice, I think.</i>

04:27.970 --> 04:29.040
For example...

04:29.900 --> 04:31.520
Crashing of waves

04:32.240 --> 04:34.770
Wait for me! Hiro-san!

04:34.940 --> 04:38.210
Catch me if you can!

04:35.250 --> 04:35.640
Woof

04:41.590 --> 04:42.410
After that...

04:42.550 --> 04:57.070
Lovey-dovey

04:42.720 --> 04:46.740
No! No! I won't take a bath unless you take one with me!

04:46.950 --> 04:49.800
Sorry Hiro-san, but I've to go to work now...

04:49.840 --> 04:54.720
No! No! If you leave now, who's going to help wash me?

04:54.840 --> 04:57.520
Oh, Hiro-san, I guess it can't be helped!

04:57.630 --> 04:58.440
And then...

04:58.920 --> 05:00.010
I'm home!

05:00.720 --> 05:02.400
Welcome back, Nowaki!

05:02.580 --> 05:04.030
Hiro-san, that outfit...!

05:04.180 --> 05:08.600
T-Today, I just thought... I'd try something different... or something like that...

05:04.240 --> 05:11.320
Lovey dovey

05:13.880 --> 05:15.610
That's absolutely impossible.

05:21.080 --> 05:21.750
Hello?

05:21.940 --> 05:23.160
Ah, it's me.

05:23.790 --> 05:26.020
Is there an envelope on the table?

05:26.190 --> 05:27.670
Let's see...

05:28.200 --> 05:29.840
Oh, there is!

05:31.110 --> 05:33.890
There are some materials in there that I need for my class...

05:34.100 --> 05:36.730
Could you bring it to the front gate of the school?

05:37.360 --> 05:39.480
Okay. I'll be right there!

05:41.550 --> 05:42.830
Nowaki!

05:52.040 --> 05:53.280
Sorry!

05:53.730 --> 05:54.910
Seriously, sorry.

05:54.910 --> 05:56.110
It's all right.

05:56.540 --> 05:58.370
I'm going to my work now anyway.

05:58.920 --> 05:59.940
Oh, yeah.

06:00.010 --> 06:04.110
I have a night shift at work, so once it ends, I'll go shopping on my way home.

06:04.370 --> 06:07.030
Hiro-san, what would you like to eat tomorrow?

06:07.590 --> 06:09.150
Let's see...

06:09.810 --> 06:12.260
I want to eat some curry-simmered fish!

06:13.120 --> 06:15.430
Professor Miyagi...

06:15.560 --> 06:18.880
Right, no flirting at the school gate!

06:18.880 --> 06:20.070
I'm not!

06:20.070 --> 06:21.340
Eh? Liar~

06:22.410 --> 06:25.440
Mister, spoiling him too much isn't good.

06:26.100 --> 06:27.780
It goes to his head immediately.

06:28.230 --> 06:30.480
<i>When</i> exactly has that ever happened!?

06:30.640 --> 06:33.640
Oh, my Hiroki has finally left the nest...

06:34.050 --> 06:36.770
Would you stop calling me by my first name!?

06:36.770 --> 06:38.590
Eh? What's the big deal, Hiroki?

06:38.610 --> 06:41.610
Why should I put up with this from you!?

06:38.880 --> 06:42.940
<i>Speaking of which, is there anyone who calls Hiroki-san by his first name?</i>

06:41.610 --> 06:42.970
That hurt!

06:42.970 --> 06:45.330
I'm gonna tell this to all the students you know!

06:45.370 --> 06:47.450
Stupid Hiroki!!

06:47.700 --> 06:49.450
Do what you want.

06:52.680 --> 06:54.230
<i>Why is he upset?</i>

06:54.930 --> 06:58.930
<i>Is being called by his first name something special for him?</i>

06:59.560 --> 07:02.010
Not "Hiro-san" but "Hiroki"...

07:03.310 --> 07:07.870
Umm, sorry! Please don't mind about it. He's always like that.

07:08.320 --> 07:10.620
For food, I'm good with anything you pick...

07:10.620 --> 07:11.400
Hiro-san!

07:12.260 --> 07:16.150
Is it okay if I call you "Hiroki" instead of "Hiro-san"?

07:18.360 --> 07:19.210
Stop it.

07:21.530 --> 07:22.800
Thanks for this.

07:26.310 --> 07:27.120
<i>Right now...</i>

07:27.970 --> 07:29.450
<i>...that hurt a bit.</i>

07:30.890 --> 07:32.950
<i>When my emotions are unsteady,</i>

07:33.440 --> 07:36.860
<i>even wounds that may seem laughably small to others,</i>

07:37.550 --> 07:40.700
<i>seem to run deep for me.</i>

07:42.720 --> 07:44.730
<i>Someone somewhere once said, </i>

07:45.200 --> 07:47.900
<i>love starts after you get together.</i>

07:48.670 --> 07:50.160
<i>That's exactly it, I believe.</i>

07:52.430 --> 07:56.930
<i>The more closer you are with someone, the more you're at the mercy of every casual remark coming from them.</i>

07:58.820 --> 08:00.130
<i>No matter how much you love,</i>

08:02.290 --> 08:05.220
<i>they will never be 100% yours.</i>

08:09.480 --> 08:10.190
<i>But...</i>

08:13.110 --> 08:14.270
<i>...but still...</i>

08:15.800 --> 08:18.540
<i>...I want to have Hiro-san all to myself.</i>

08:20.040 --> 08:23.880
<i> I felt a bit hurt when he refused to let me call him by his first name because</i>

08:25.200 --> 08:28.080
<i>I thought it was natural for him to allow me to do that.</i>

08:34.670 --> 08:37.290
Oh, hello! Welcome!

08:37.460 --> 08:39.980
U-Um, excuse me.

08:41.140 --> 08:44.750
Um, can I get a bouquet for about 3000 Yen?

08:45.030 --> 08:46.000
You can.

08:46.420 --> 08:47.700
Is it a present.

08:47.850 --> 08:49.120
Ah, yes.

08:50.480 --> 08:52.240
What kind would you like?

08:52.640 --> 08:54.500
Let's see...

08:55.110 --> 08:57.090
Roses! Roses would be nice!

08:57.450 --> 08:59.020
Okay, roses it is.

08:59.450 --> 09:02.630
<i>Because you love them you absolutely don't want their dismay.</i>

09:03.880 --> 09:06.750
<i>You always want to be their number one.</i>

09:09.410 --> 09:10.690
Thank you very much.

09:10.990 --> 09:12.790
<i>I wonder if it's a present for his girlfriend.</i>

09:15.000 --> 09:16.760
<i>He seems so innocent and naive.</i>

09:18.370 --> 09:24.050
<i>There's nothing wrong in putting your heart and effort into pleasing the person you love.</i>

09:25.040 --> 09:26.470
<i>I do believe that but...</i>

09:28.780 --> 09:31.560
<i>...if one is uncertain, its best to ask the other directly, I think.</i>

09:33.350 --> 09:37.290
<i>Am I really special to Hiro-san?</i>

09:38.560 --> 09:42.400
<i>What rank do I hold in his heart?</i>

09:47.280 --> 09:50.160
<i>I can never ask anything so childish.</i>

09:51.220 --> 09:54.220
<i>I don't want to show my uncool side in front of him.</i>

09:56.060 --> 09:57.090
<i>Or...</i>

09:58.490 --> 09:59.620
<i>...Or...</i>

09:59.840 --> 10:06.060
<i>...do I even have the confidence to imagine what his answer would be?</i>

10:07.560 --> 10:08.800
<i>Right now...</i>

10:10.640 --> 10:14.840
<i>...I wonder if I am someone even worthy of Hiro-san's love in the first place.</i>

10:23.480 --> 10:24.480
Good work.

10:24.550 --> 10:26.570
Oh, good work.

10:27.860 --> 10:29.450
How's your residency going?

10:29.920 --> 10:31.360
Getting used to it a little?

10:32.120 --> 10:34.530
There's many things I'm still not sure about...

10:36.590 --> 10:37.310
Umm...

10:37.440 --> 10:38.000
Hmm?

10:39.440 --> 10:44.350
What level should one have to reach, to call it number one?

10:47.080 --> 10:48.600
Let's see...

10:48.960 --> 10:52.930
The moment you think you are number one, it's the start line for you.

10:53.490 --> 10:54.460
And the goal?

10:54.660 --> 10:57.180
Well, finding it before you die would be nice.

11:01.220 --> 11:03.010
<i>They can just assign points then...</i>

11:05.270 --> 11:10.750
<i>If I knew getting these many points would be fail or pass grade, it would be so convenient.</i>

11:12.240 --> 11:13.420
<i>If that were so,</i>

11:13.910 --> 11:17.160
<i>I could know how long do I need to keep chasing Hiro-san.</i>

11:17.790 --> 11:20.270
<i>I could know when I would be his equal.</i>

11:20.710 --> 11:24.150
<i>Quickly, I want to catch up to Hiro-san.</i>

11:30.140 --> 11:31.620
Hiro-san
1 new mail

11:38.440 --> 11:39.440
Hiro-san!

11:44.050 --> 11:46.320
Thanks for the message.

11:46.620 --> 11:47.520
Yeah.

11:48.090 --> 11:49.850
Are you okay with work?

11:50.140 --> 11:52.050
It got over just now.

11:52.330 --> 11:53.340
I see.

11:56.700 --> 11:57.590
What is it?

11:58.050 --> 11:58.940
Nothing.

12:00.900 --> 12:02.120
What's the matter?

12:02.380 --> 12:04.490
You coming to pick me up is sort of rare.

12:04.560 --> 12:07.230
Nothing, I just felt like eating out for breakfast.

12:07.230 --> 12:10.130
Then, there's a family restaurant up ahead we can go to.

12:15.100 --> 12:16.870
Hey, Nowaki...

12:17.330 --> 12:17.800
Yeah?

12:18.400 --> 12:19.530
Hiroki!

12:23.050 --> 12:25.470
Gah! Akihiko!

12:25.570 --> 12:27.960
Why do I have to run into you first thing in the morning!?

12:28.100 --> 12:29.980
That should be my line.

12:31.440 --> 12:32.480
<i>"Hiroki"...</i>

12:33.560 --> 12:37.500
So, I received some peaches from your mom.

12:37.580 --> 12:38.640
Peaches?

12:38.730 --> 12:40.910
I didn't receive any from her.

12:41.000 --> 12:43.230
What is she thinking!?

12:43.400 --> 12:45.360
Probably something about your terrible manners.

12:45.460 --> 12:46.430
What!?

12:46.430 --> 12:47.470
Hey, don't climb up!

12:47.470 --> 12:49.120
Shut up! You and your cocky attitude!

12:49.770 --> 12:50.930
<i>"Hiroki"...</i>

12:51.300 --> 12:54.800
<i>When anyone else called him that, he'd get upset right away.</i>

12:56.960 --> 13:00.500
<i>I can't stand myself having these childish thoughts...</i>

13:02.960 --> 13:05.510
Want to come over to fetch the peaches? I'll give you a ride.

13:06.820 --> 13:07.660
<i>But...</i>

13:08.290 --> 13:09.440
No need!

13:10.380 --> 13:11.070
Hiroki!

13:11.070 --> 13:12.400
Wa-Wait!

13:14.660 --> 13:17.060
Nowaki! What's with you suddenly?

13:17.220 --> 13:19.070
Hey, Nowaki!

13:22.640 --> 13:24.320
What the hell!?

13:24.930 --> 13:29.010
Peaches, persimmons, apples, grapes- whatever you want, I'll buy it for you!

13:29.220 --> 13:30.170
What?

13:30.240 --> 13:33.870
By the way, I asked why did you do that when people are having a conversation?

13:34.030 --> 13:35.320
Because that...

13:35.790 --> 13:37.750
You, cut it out!

13:38.340 --> 13:40.130
Stop behaving like a kid!

13:43.630 --> 13:44.900
<i>A 4 year gap...</i>

13:45.530 --> 13:46.340
<i>...is huge.</i>

14:15.760 --> 14:17.380
Did something happen?

14:18.200 --> 14:20.380
Since earlier you've been kinda weird.

14:21.560 --> 14:24.070
Sorry. It's nothing.

14:24.390 --> 14:27.530
Nowaki, look at me when you're speaking.

14:27.880 --> 14:29.090
I'm sorry.

14:29.590 --> 14:31.330
Really, it's nothing.

14:32.320 --> 14:33.710
<i>I couldn't tell...</i>

14:40.370 --> 14:41.400
<i>This person...</i>

14:44.060 --> 14:45.140
<i>...I want him...</i>

14:48.400 --> 14:49.600
<i>...all for myself.</i>

14:56.630 --> 14:58.000
<i>Make a mess of him...</i>

14:58.860 --> 14:59.780
<i>...and of myself too.</i>

15:01.900 --> 15:03.070
Nowaki...?

15:03.890 --> 15:06.640
<i>Mark him all over as mine.</i>

15:07.680 --> 15:09.240
Nowaki, stop it!

15:07.840 --> 15:10.080
Hiroki, Hiroki...

15:09.510 --> 15:10.250
Here is...

15:10.320 --> 15:11.170
Hiroki!

15:11.650 --> 15:12.660
What? Stop!

15:12.140 --> 15:13.980
Hiroki, Hiroki...

15:12.920 --> 15:13.980
Nowaki!

15:14.220 --> 15:15.200
I said stop!

15:15.190 --> 15:15.900
Hiroki...

15:16.790 --> 15:18.760
That way of calling out...

15:17.680 --> 15:18.630
Hiroki...

15:19.020 --> 15:21.360
I said stop using that way of calling me!

15:21.430 --> 15:22.760
Why is that?

15:24.350 --> 15:26.960
Usami-san was calling you that as if it was normal.

15:27.070 --> 15:27.780
What?

15:28.400 --> 15:31.740
Is there a reason that it's okay if he calls you that but I can't!?

15:32.890 --> 15:34.460
What are you saying?

15:34.460 --> 15:36.580
What is it that I'm lacking!?

15:36.630 --> 15:37.270
Hey!

15:37.270 --> 15:39.900
If I know what I'm lacking, I'll fix it immediately!

15:39.900 --> 15:41.680
Just calm down a bit!

15:41.780 --> 15:42.980
So I...!

15:42.980 --> 15:43.990
Nowaki!

15:50.030 --> 15:53.570
What are you so irritated about?

15:53.990 --> 15:57.370
Akihiko's not the only one who calls me by my name.

15:57.640 --> 15:59.070
My parents do too.

15:59.750 --> 16:03.110
So... such a thing...

16:04.000 --> 16:04.770
What?

16:05.230 --> 16:08.070
Wait, is this why you've been so weird lately?

16:08.780 --> 16:09.970
<i>This is the worst.</i>

16:11.340 --> 16:13.180
<i>I showed my most uncool side</i>

16:14.080 --> 16:16.560
<i>to the one person I never wanted to show to.</i>

16:17.020 --> 16:19.700
Uh, Um...

16:20.540 --> 16:22.560
...that is... sorry.

16:24.150 --> 16:26.270
Correct me if I'm wrong,

16:26.800 --> 16:32.460
but does this have to do with something you said before, about surpassing me or catching up to me?

16:37.420 --> 16:41.350
Um... I was wondering about telling this to you before...

16:44.540 --> 16:46.000
You don't have to surpass me!

16:47.250 --> 16:48.740
Try thinking about it,

16:48.740 --> 16:52.880
I've lived 4 years more than you, so it's obvious that I'll be a little ahead of you in life.

16:53.290 --> 16:58.800
That's why if I let myself fall behind you, my pride won't let me accept it.

16:59.000 --> 17:00.450
A-And...

17:00.530 --> 17:08.200
To be connected to you, I want to leave some conditions... or so I was thinking...

17:08.580 --> 17:12.580
Sorry, I myself can't understand what I am saying...

17:12.880 --> 17:16.410
Uh, no no! I do think you're working very hard. Yeah.

17:17.540 --> 17:19.930
I'm saying so, so there's no doubt about it.

17:20.300 --> 17:21.170
So...

17:22.290 --> 17:24.720
...sort of... I...

17:25.180 --> 17:27.290
...love you.

17:28.060 --> 17:30.480
O-Or something like that...!

17:31.070 --> 17:33.940
Ha! Ha! Ha! You could never pull of a line like that, could you?

17:34.250 --> 17:36.160
This is what it means to be an adult!

17:40.580 --> 17:41.860
<i>I love him...</i>

17:44.050 --> 17:46.850
Nowaki, I'm cold.

17:47.920 --> 17:49.340
<i>...really...</i>

17:50.290 --> 17:51.580
<i>...hopelessly...</i>

17:53.190 --> 17:53.730
Yes.

18:07.300 --> 18:10.190
I thought you didn't like it when I touched you.

18:11.650 --> 18:13.430
W-Why?

18:13.510 --> 18:16.520
Because no matter what I did, you never responded.

18:16.800 --> 18:22.500
So then what about the have-a-good-day kiss, goodnight kiss, welcome-back kiss...

18:22.500 --> 18:24.870
Which era's newly weds are we?

18:25.440 --> 18:28.290
I can guess exactly what's going through your head!

18:28.380 --> 18:28.890
Eh?

18:29.260 --> 18:32.760
Like taking a bath together, washing each other, making out in the bathtub,

18:32.760 --> 18:35.540
or dress up in a yukata and watch the fireworks from the veranda and make out.

18:35.540 --> 18:37.460
You head's full of those thoughts, isn't it?

18:37.460 --> 18:40.760
You're embarassing! You pervert!

18:41.270 --> 18:43.330
That's why I...

18:45.840 --> 18:46.680
<i>What's this?</i>

18:48.280 --> 18:51.640
Sorry. I didn't think about any of it.

18:52.560 --> 18:53.690
I understand!

18:53.870 --> 18:55.980
Hiro-san, you want to do all that, don't you!?

18:56.310 --> 18:57.840
That's wrong!!

18:57.920 --> 18:59.010
I'll do it!

18:59.010 --> 19:00.600
I'll do a thorough job at it!

19:00.600 --> 19:04.570
Why do you always insist on doing things that piss me off!?

19:08.720 --> 19:09.520
<i>I...</i>

19:10.040 --> 19:13.320
<i>...for the sake of the person I love, will do anything.</i>

19:14.610 --> 19:15.860
<i>So I'm sorry.</i>

19:16.460 --> 19:19.200
<i>Hiro-san, told me that I don't need to surpass him, but...</i>

19:19.920 --> 19:22.820
<i>...in order to stay connected to Hiro-san, I...</i>

19:23.550 --> 19:26.640
<i>...so that Hiro-san will always say that he loves me...</i>

19:27.090 --> 19:28.320
<i>...I'll do anything.</i>

19:31.120 --> 19:32.560
I love you, Hiro-san.

19:37.010 --> 19:39.020
<i>...really hopelessly...</i>

19:43.840 --> 19:47.560
Nowaki! You!! I told you to wake me up, didn't I!?

19:47.800 --> 19:49.150
I tried to...

19:49.520 --> 19:50.800
...25 times.

19:50.880 --> 19:53.720
Liar! I don't remember at all!

19:54.040 --> 19:55.720
Would you like to have some  breakfast before you go?

19:55.840 --> 19:58.000
Sorry. I'll grab something on the way.

19:58.090 --> 19:58.830
Hiro-san!

20:10.820 --> 20:11.760
<i>I see...</i>

20:12.780 --> 20:15.500
<i>Hiro-san was shy about this, then.</i>

20:15.860 --> 20:19.300
You! Again you're thinking of something unnecessary, isn't it?

20:19.410 --> 20:21.090
Nothing like that.

20:21.160 --> 20:23.070
Leave it! I'm going to be late.

20:24.560 --> 20:25.640
You've forgotten...

20:25.670 --> 20:26.670
Nothing.

20:29.570 --> 20:33.930
Oh, that's right. You were getting all worked up over calling me by my name and all that before right?

20:34.480 --> 20:36.320
Let me tell you one thing.

20:36.720 --> 20:37.230
Eh?

20:38.720 --> 20:40.750
I have a very special name.

20:41.340 --> 20:44.080
And that's something only that one single person can say.

20:44.320 --> 20:46.270
Eh? What's that?

20:48.080 --> 20:49.020
Hiro-san.

20:54.160 --> 20:55.920
That's all. See ya later.

20:56.720 --> 20:58.560
U-Um, Hiro-san!

21:00.100 --> 21:03.140
Um, the fireworks season is over already,

21:03.290 --> 21:05.700
so for starters lets have a bath together.

21:08.160 --> 21:09.520
Shut up!!

21:09.560 --> 21:12.830
Are you stupid!? What are you blabbering about first thing in the morning!?

21:12.980 --> 21:14.310
Hiro-san, Hiro-san!

21:14.310 --> 21:17.040
Shut up! You brat!!

21:16.470 --> 21:17.100
Hiro-san!

21:18.710 --> 21:22.430
<i>Looking from anyone's viewpoint, even laughably tiny things to be happy about,</i>

21:19.090 --> 21:19.840
Hiro-san!

21:22.500 --> 21:27.450
<i>for a simple man of simples tastes like me, seem like the greatest happiness of my life.</i>

21:40.900 --> 21:46.040
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

21:40.900 --> 21:46.040
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:46.170 --> 21:51.430
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:46.170 --> 21:51.430
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

21:51.780 --> 21:56.800
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

21:51.780 --> 21:56.800
You doubled all my happiness,

21:56.800 --> 22:03.490
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

21:56.800 --> 22:03.490
and halved all my sadness.

22:03.600 --> 22:08.600
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

22:03.600 --> 22:08.600
No matter what path I walk in the future,

22:09.000 --> 22:13.280
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

22:09.000 --> 22:13.280
will surely lead to you.

22:13.280 --> 22:16.040
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

22:13.280 --> 22:16.040
You're there up ahead of me,

22:16.040 --> 22:18.900
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

22:16.040 --> 22:18.900
I'm there ahead of you,

22:18.900 --> 22:24.170
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

22:18.900 --> 22:24.170
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

22:24.170 --> 22:30.070
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

22:24.170 --> 22:30.070
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

22:30.660 --> 22:35.140
mou doko he mo ikanaide

22:30.660 --> 22:35.140
Hey, don't go anywhere.

22:35.140 --> 22:40.600
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

22:35.140 --> 22:40.600
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:40.600 --> 22:45.990
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:40.600 --> 22:45.990
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:45.990 --> 22:51.810
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:45.990 --> 22:51.810
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

22:52.200 --> 22:57.490
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

22:52.200 --> 22:57.490
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

23:09.650 --> 23:11.290
It sure is beautiful.

23:11.670 --> 23:16.320
Yeah. But Hiro-san is much more beautiful.

23:33.010 --> 23:34.360
<i>A dream?</i>

23:39.740 --> 23:46.350
Raws: BDRIP (from nyaa.se)
Translation: aarinfantasy
Timing, Typesetting, Minor script editing and Encoding: asckj1

23:56.970 --> 23:59.990
From within the lie comes the truth
